@startuml "Bridge - Notifications (Variations) - Class Diagram"
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
title Two variations — who chooses the implementor, and who owns it


package "variation 1 - a factory chooses (GoF implementation issue 2)" {
  interface ChannelFactory {
    + channelFor(Recipient) : NotificationChannel
  }
  class PreferenceChannelFactory {
    - channels : Map<ChannelKind, NotificationChannel>
    + channelFor(Recipient) : NotificationChannel
    + register(kind, channel) : PreferenceChannelFactory
  }
  class NotificationService {
    + send(kind, to, message) : DeliveryResult
  }
  ChannelFactory <|.. PreferenceChannelFactory
  NotificationService o--> ChannelFactory

  note bottom of NotificationService
    The caller names <b>neither</b> a channel class
    nor a combination class. The recipient's
    stored preference decides, at run time.
  end note
}

package "variation 2 - sharing one implementor (issue 3)" {
  class PooledChannel {
    - inner : NotificationChannel
    - users : int
    - messages : int
    + acquire() : PooledChannel
  }
  note bottom of PooledChannel
    One SMTP connection serving many
    notifications.
    <b>Cost:</b> shared state — thread safety,
    and its failures are everybody's.
  end note
}

note as N1
  Neither variation changes the pattern. Each answers a question
  the classic version leaves to whoever writes `new`.
end note

@enduml
